WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.321 --> 00:00:01.154
(peaceful music)

00:00:01.154 --> 00:00:03.060
- [Woman] The idyllic
islands of French Polynesia

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:05.270
may seem like a relaxing paradise

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:08.210
of pristine reefs and clear waters,

00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:10.563
but take a dip below the surface.

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:13.893
Are you ready for a swim?

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:20.770
Fakarava is a rectangular shaped atoll

00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:24.223
located in French Polynesia
in the South Pacific Ocean.

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:27.290
The southern parts of Farkarava

00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:29.530
is known as the gray shark wall

00:00:29.530 --> 00:00:31.520
due to having the highest concentration

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:34.386
of gray reef sharks in the world.

00:00:34.386 --> 00:00:38.350
Since 2006, the sharks have
been protected from fishing,

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:41.003
which is attributed to
their population increase.

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:44.820
During the day the
sharks are fairly docile

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:48.073
and conserve energy, ready
to hunt their pray at night.

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:51.890
Although the exact number of sharks

00:00:51.890 --> 00:00:56.890
found Fakarava is uncertain,
with only 650 human residents,

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.223
it's likely the people are outnumbered.

00:01:06.767 --> 00:01:09.350
(digital gong)

